.\" sballd-wrapper manual page
.TH SBALLD-WRAPPER 8 "2026-10-14" "sball-addition 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sballd-wrapper \- run the pre-quorate hooks and start the PVM service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sballd-wrapper
[\fIsballd arguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sballd-wrapper
replaces
.BR sballd (8)
as the entry point of the service unit
.RB ( "
ExecStart=/usr/bin/sballd-wrapper
" ).
It runs the pre-quorate hooks, starts the post-quorate watcher and finally
.BR exec s
the real daemon with the original arguments, so the pid, the signal handling
and the systemd behaviour stay identical to a plain
.B sballd
start.
.PP
A failing hook with
.B ON_FAIL=abort
(stop the phase) aborts the start: the node stays out of the cluster instead of
joining half configured. Errors of the hook system itself (missing binary,
broken configuration, invalid hook set) only produce a warning \(em the daemon
is started anyway \(em unless
.B SBALL_ADDITION_REQUIRED=1
is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SBALLD_BIN
The real daemon. Defaults to
.I /usr/sbin/sballd.real
when it exists (shim installation), otherwise
.IR /usr/sbin/sballd .
.TP
.B SBALL_ADDITION_BIN
The sball-addition CLI (default
.IR /usr/bin/sball-addition ).
.TP
.B SBALL_ADDITION_WRAPPER_ARGS
Extra CLI arguments, for example
.IR "\-\-log\-level=debug" .
.TP
.B SBALL_ADDITION_REQUIRED
Set to 1 to abort the start when the hook system itself is broken (default 0 =
fail open).
.TP
.B SBALL_ADDITION_SKIP_WRAPPER
Set to 1 to start the daemon without running any hook (emergency switch).
.TP
.B SBALL_ADDITION_LOG
Log file mentioned in the messages printed on failure (default
.IR /var/log/sball-addition/sball-addition.log ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sball-addition/hooks.d/pre-quorate.d
Hooks executed before the daemon starts.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/sballd.service.d/sball-addition.conf
The drop-in that points
.B sballd.service
at this wrapper.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the service the way an upgrade or a reboot would:
.PP
.RS
systemctl restart sballd.service
.RE
.PP
Preview the hooks without starting anything:
.PP
.RS
sball-addition run-phase pre-quorate \-\-dry-run
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sball-addition (8),
.BR sball-node-verify (8),
.BR sball-rollout (8),
.BR systemd.service (5)
